NAME
       date - print or set the system date and time

SYNOPSIS
       date [-u] [-d @SECONDS | -r FILE] [+FORMAT]
       date [-u] MMDDhhmm[[CC]YY][.ss]

DESCRIPTION
       Prints the current time in the local time zone, using the
       default format "%a %b %e %H:%M:%S %Z %Y" or FORMAT, which takes
       the conversions of strftime(3).

       Given MMDDhhmm with an optional year and seconds, sets the
       system clock to that local time instead. Setting the clock
       needs the right to change the time.

OPTIONS
       -u          Use Coordinated Universal Time instead of the local
                   time zone.
       -d @SECONDS Show the time SECONDS after the Epoch.
       -r FILE     Show the modification time of FILE.

ENVIRONMENT
       TZ          The time zone, as a zone name such as Europe/Berlin
                   from /usr/share/zoneinfo or a POSIX rule such as
                   EST5EDT,M3.2.0,M11.1.0. Without it /etc/localtime is
                   used.

FILES
       /etc/localtime        the system time zone
       /usr/share/zoneinfo   the time zone database

SEE ALSO
       ntpdate(1), uptime(1), strftime(3)
